Normalize fixed Gaussian blurs and add parameterized gaussian_blur

Roadmap v0.3.0 items 0 and 7.

Item 0 (breaking): gaussian_blur_3x3 / gaussian_blur_5x5 are now
normalized (kernel sums to 1) and preserve brightness, matching box_blur_*
and every mainstream library. Normalization lives in the
SeparableKernel::gaussian_3 / gaussian_5 factories ([0.25,0.5,0.25] and
[0.0625,0.25,0.375,0.25,0.0625]). The raw integer kernels [1,2,1] (sum 16)
and [1,4,6,4,1] (sum 256) are unchanged and remain at the
Neighborhood::gaussian_3x3 / gaussian_5x5 + gaussian_1d_* layer, where the
caller owns the scale. Doctests and tests asserting the old x16/x256
scaling were updated, including tests/end_to_end.rs.

Item 7: gaussian_blur(image, sigma, border) and
gaussian_blur_with(.., truncate, ..) (plus _into variants) derive a
normalized separable kernel from sigma over the existing
convolve_separable_raw engine. Kernel generator exposed at the image layer:
gaussian_kernel_1d, gaussian_kernel_size, GaussianKernel1D, MAX_RADIUS (64).
Radius = round(truncate*sigma) (SciPy/scikit-image parity), default
truncate = 4.0. sigma <= 0 and over-radius sigma panic (Tier 3). The fixed
3x3/5x5 paths are kept as fast const-sized convenience functions.

Adds 25 tests (kernel invariants, impulse response, separability vs full
2D convolution, monotonic smoothing, into-variants, panics). Full suite,
doctests, clippy, and rustfmt all pass.
